{
  "_readme": [
    "The invented prospect roster behind the demo business's go-to-market pipeline.",
    "",
    "DATA ONLY, ON PURPOSE. Two very different programs read this file — the seed script that writes",
    "these rows into a loopback kernel, and cloud/scripts/demo-faces.mjs which draws a monogram avatar",
    "per row — and the one thing that must never drift between them is the roster itself. A slug that",
    "exists here and not in the avatar output is a broken image on a recording; a slug that exists in",
    "the avatar output and not here is dead weight in the repo. One file, both readers.",
    "",
    "EVERY NAME AND EVERY COMPANY BELOW IS INVENTED. Domains are all `.example`, which RFC 2606",
    "reserves precisely so a fixture can never name a real host, and no person here exists — the",
    "avatars are generated monograms, not photographs of anybody. The world is the one Ridgeline Books",
    "already lives in (small service businesses: bakeries, studios, clinics, workshops), but these are",
    "PROSPECTS, deliberately disjoint from the client list in seed-demo.ts.",
    "",
    "WHAT IS SEEDED HERE IS BUSINESS STATE, NOT AGENT OUTPUT. A stage, a due time and a name are facts",
    "about a pipeline and the seed is allowed to state them. There is deliberately no `provenance` on a",
    "person: provenance is the record of enrichment attempts and what each one cost, and writing one",
    "would put invented dollar figures on the screen whose entire claim is that the figures are real.",
    "The `paused_reason` strings are copied VERBATIM out of kernel/harness/src/gtm/sequence.ts and",
    "pacing.ts — the sequencer's own sentences — rather than paraphrased, for the same reason.",
    "",
    "`dueInHours` is fractional everywhere so the board's to-the-minute clock prints irregular times",
    "(14:37, not 14:00). The kernel jitters every real interval by ±40% and the irregularity IS the",
    "proof it is not a cron; a seed that landed on round hours would quietly undo that."
  ],
